# File Organization Standards

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/                 # Next.js app directory
│   ├── (auth)/         # Route group
│   ├── (dashboard)/    # Route group
│   ├── api/            # API routes
│   ├── layout.tsx
│   └── page.tsx
├── components/
│   ├── ui/             # Reusable UI components
│   │   ├── Button.tsx
│   │   ├── Input.tsx
│   │   └── Card.tsx
│   └── features/       # Feature-specific components
│       ├── auth/
│       └── dashboard/
├── hooks/              # Custom React hooks
│   ├── useAuth.ts
│   └── useDebounce.ts
├── lib/                # Utilities and helpers
│   ├── api.ts
│   ├── utils.ts
│   └── constants.ts
├── server/             # Server-side code
│   ├── db.ts
│   └── actions/
├── types/              # Shared TypeScript types
│   └── index.ts
└── styles/             # Global styles
    └── globals.css
```

## Naming Conventions

### Files
- **Components**: PascalCase - `UserProfile.tsx`, `Button.tsx`
- **Hooks**: camelCase with 'use' prefix - `useAuth.ts`, `useDebounce.ts`
- **Utilities**: camelCase - `formatDate.ts`, `api.ts`
- **Types**: camelCase or PascalCase - `types.ts`, `User.types.ts`
- **Tests**: Match source file - `Button.test.tsx`

### Variables and Functions
- **Components**: PascalCase - `UserProfile`, `Button`
- **Functions**: camelCase - `fetchUser`, `formatDate`
- **Hooks**: camelCase with 'use' - `useAuth`, `useDebounce`
- **Constants**: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE - `API_BASE_URL`, `MAX_RETRY_COUNT`
- **Types/Interfaces**: PascalCase - `User`, `UserProfile`, `ApiResponse`

## Component File Structure

### Single Component File:
```typescript
// 1. Imports - React, Next.js, external, internal
import { useState } from 'react';
import Link from 'next/link';
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils';
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button';

// 2. Types/Interfaces
interface UserCardProps {
  user: User;
  onEdit?: () => void;
}

// 3. Component
export function UserCard({ user, onEdit }: UserCardProps) {
  const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = useState(false);
  
  return (
    <div>
      {/* JSX */}
    </div>
  );
}

// 4. Sub-components (if small)
function UserAvatar({ src }: { src: string }) {
  return <img src={src} alt="Avatar" />;
}
```

### Multiple Related Components (Index Pattern):
```
components/
└── UserCard/
    ├── index.tsx         # Main component + exports
    ├── UserAvatar.tsx    # Sub-component
    ├── UserBio.tsx       # Sub-component
    ├── types.ts          # Local types
    └── UserCard.test.tsx # Tests
```

## Import Organization

### Order:
1. React and Next.js
2. Third-party libraries
3. Internal modules (@/...)
4. Relative imports
5. Types (import type)
6. Styles

### Example:
```typescript
// React/Next.js
import { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { useRouter } from 'next/navigation';

// Third-party
import { z } from 'zod';
import { cn } from 'clsx';

// Internal
import { Button } from '@/components/ui/Button';
import { fetchUser } from '@/lib/api';

// Relative
import { UserAvatar } from './UserAvatar';

// Types
import type { User } from '@/types';

// Styles
import './styles.css';
```

## Feature-Based Organization (for larger projects)

```
features/
├── authentication/
│   ├── components/
│   │   ├── LoginForm.tsx
│   │   └── RegisterForm.tsx
│   ├── hooks/
│   │   └── useAuth.ts
│   ├── api/
│   │   └── authApi.ts
│   ├── types/
│   │   └── auth.types.ts
│   └── tests/
│       └── LoginForm.test.tsx
└── user-profile/
    ├── components/
    ├── hooks/
    ├── api/
    └── types/
```

## Exports

### Use Named Exports:
```typescript
// ✅ Good
export function Button() {}
export const UserCard = () => {};

// ❌ Avoid
export default Button;
```

### Exception - Next.js Pages:
```typescript
// app/page.tsx - default export required
export default function HomePage() {}
```

## Code Generation Preferences

When generating files:
1. Follow the project structure above
2. Use named exports (except Next.js pages)
3. Organize imports in the specified order
4. Use proper naming conventions
5. Co-locate related files
6. Keep components under 200 lines
7. Extract sub-components when needed
